  "date_building_work_completed_under_previous_permission": null,
  "lapsed_date": "20/10/2029",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Occupier",
    "The development must be begun not later than the expiration of three years beginning with the date hereof.\r\rReason: To comply with Section 91 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990, as amended.",
    "The floodlighting hereby approved shall be installed and maintained strictly in accordance with the approved lighting design specifications and documents, including LP260301 Lighting Design Report - Rev 6 (Lumineux, 22 September 2026), LumiSport Series Specification, and Drawing 300626.SUTTON.\r\rReason: To protect local ecology, habitats, and protected species (bats), to comply with Policy 26 and Policy 28 of the Sutton Local Plan (2018) and Policy G6 of the London Plan (2021).",
    "The floodlighting hereby permitted shall only be illuminated between the hours of:\r\r06:30 to 22:00 Mondays to Fridays;\r\r08:00 to 20:00 Saturdays, Sundays, and Bank/Public Holidays.\r\rOutside of these permitted hours, the floodlighting shall be fully extinguished.\r\rReason: To safeguard the living conditions and residential amenities of nearby occupiers and to prevent light spill affecting local wildlife, to comply with Policy 26 and Policy 29 of the Sutton Local Plan (2018).",
    "Prior to the commencement of the development a Construction Management Plan shall be submitted to and agreed by the Local Planning Authority outlining measures that will be taken to control dust, noise, contaminated land, and other environmental impacts of the development.\r\rReason: To safeguard neighbour amenity and environmental health during construction, to comply with Policy 29 and Policy 36 of the Sutton Local Plan (2018).",
    "If during implementation of this development, contamination is encountered which has not previously been identified, the additional contamination shall be fully assessed and a specific contaminated land assessment and associated remedial strategy shall be submitted to and agreed in writing by the Local Planning Authority before the additional remediation works are carried out. The agreed strategy shall be implemented in full prior to completion of the development hereby approved.\r\rReason: There is possibility that not all contamination has been identified by the investigation. If contamination is discovered during the development this will need to managed appropriately so that there are no remaining unacceptable risks to human health or the environment and to comply with Policy 34 of the Sutton Local Plan (2018).",
    "The development must be carried out in accordance with the provisions of the Fire Safety Exception Statement (Date: July 16, 2026).\r\rReason: To ensure that the development incorporates the necessary fire safety measures in accordance with the Mayor's London Plan Policy D12."
  ],
